}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/services/social-growth/settings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "isEnabled": true,
    "activeProvider": "exosupplier",
    "userMarkupPercent": 15,
    "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
    "usdToNgnRate": 1600,
    "roundingMode": "ceil",
    "userPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 1000, "markupPercent": 15 },
      { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 5001, "maxCost": 15000, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 15001, "maxCost": 50000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 50001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 3 }
    ],
    "vendorPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 1000, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 5001, "maxCost": 15000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 15001, "maxCost": 50000, "markupPercent": 3 },
      { "minCost": 50001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 2 }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  # Admin Update Social Growth Settings

  Admin uses this endpoint to update social growth provider and pricing settings.

  You can send all fields at once or only the fields that changed. The backend saves only recognized fields.

  ## Endpoint

  `PATCH /api/v1/admin/services/social-growth/settings`

  ## Authentication

  Admin JWT required:

  ```txt
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
  ```

  The logged-in user must have:

  ```json
  {
    "role": "admin"
  }
  ```

  Normal users and vendors must not call this endpoint.

  ## Body Fields

  `isEnabled`
  Use `true` to allow purchases or `false` to disable social growth.

  `activeProvider`
  Provider the backend should use for service list, quote, order placement, and order status checks. Supported values are `exosupplier` and `vheeboost`.

  `usdToNgnRate`
  Exchange rate used when provider pricing is returned in USD. Example: if USD 1 should become NGN 1600, send `1600`.

  `userMarkupPercent`
  Fallback percentage markup for normal users if no pricing tier matches the provider cost.

  `vendorMarkupPercent`
  Fallback percentage markup for active vendors if no pricing tier matches the provider cost.

  `userPricingTiers`
  Percentage rules for normal users based on provider cost.

  `vendorPricingTiers`
  Percentage rules for vendors based on provider cost.

  `roundingMode`
  Use `ceil` to round up to the next naira. Use `round` for normal rounding.

  ## Full Example Body

  ```json
  {
    "isEnabled": true,
    "activeProvider": "exosupplier",
    "userMarkupPercent": 15,
    "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
    "usdToNgnRate": 1600,
    "roundingMode": "ceil",
    "userPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 1000, "markupPercent": 15 },
      { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 5001, "maxCost": 15000, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 15001, "maxCost": 50000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 50001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 3 }
    ],
    "vendorPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 1000, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 5001, "maxCost": 15000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 15001, "maxCost": 50000, "markupPercent": 3 },
      { "minCost": 50001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 2 }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Partial Update Examples

  Disable social growth temporarily:

  ```json
  {
    "isEnabled": false
  }
  ```

  Switch provider:

  ```json
  {
    "activeProvider": "vheeboost"
  }
  ```

  Update only the USD exchange rate:

  ```json
  {
    "usdToNgnRate": 1650
  }
  ```

  ## Tier Rules Explained

  Each tier has:

  `minCost`
  Lowest provider cost for the tier.

  `maxCost`
  Highest provider cost for the tier. Use `null` for the final "and above" tier.

  `markupPercent`
  Percentage added on top of provider cost.

  Example:

  ```json
  { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 10 }
  ```

  This means if the provider cost is between NGN 1001 and NGN 5000, the user price is provider cost plus 10%.

  The backend sorts valid tiers by `minCost`. Invalid tiers are ignored. A tier is invalid if:

  - `minCost` is missing or below `0`
  - `maxCost` is below `minCost`
  - `markupPercent` is missing, below `0`, or above `100`

  ## Recommended MVP Tier Structure

  Normal users:

  ```txt
  cost 0 - 1000        => 15%
  cost 1001 - 5000     => 10%
  cost 5001 - 15000    => 7%
  cost 15001 - 50000   => 5%
  cost 50001 and above => 3%
  ```

  Vendors:

  ```txt
  cost 0 - 1000        => 10%
  cost 1001 - 5000     => 7%
  cost 5001 - 15000    => 5%
  cost 15001 - 50000   => 3%
  cost 50001 and above => 2%
  ```

  ## Expected Success Response

  Status: `200 OK`

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Social growth service settings updated successfully",
    "settings": {
      "id": "66...",
      "service": "social_growth",
      "isEnabled": true,
      "activeProvider": "exosupplier",
      "availableProviders": [
        {
          "name": "exosupplier",
          "available": true
        },
        {
          "name": "vheeboost",
          "available": true
        }
      ],
      "userMarkupPercent": 15,
      "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
      "usdToNgnRate": 1600,
      "userPricingTiers": [
        { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 1000, "markupPercent": 15 },
        { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 10 }
      ],
      "vendorPricingTiers": [
        { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 1000, "markupPercent": 10 },
        { "minCost": 1001, "maxCost": 5000, "markupPercent": 7 }
      ],
      "roundingMode": "ceil",
      "updatedBy": "66...",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-07T08:00:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-07T08:30:00.000Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Common Errors

  No recognized field was sent:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "No valid social growth settings were provided. Send JSON fields like activeProvider, userPricingTiers, or vendorPricingTiers."
  }
  ```

  Unsupported provider:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "SocialGrowthServiceSetting validation failed: activeProvider: `unknown` is not a valid enum value for path `activeProvider`."
  }
  ```

  User is not admin:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Not authorized for this role"
  }
  ```

  ## Admin Dashboard Notes

  Fetch current settings first with `GET /api/v1/admin/services/social-growth/settings`.

  Save only when the admin clicks a clear save button.

  After saving, use the `settings` object from the response or call the GET endpoint again.

  The frontend user app should not call this endpoint. Only the admin dashboard should call it.
}
